I'm here for the cruSt.
我就是冲着饼边来的。

151
00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:56.300
And then I want you to know that I'm talking all crusts, deep dish crust, medium, thin crust
然后我想让你知道我说的是各种饼边，深盘厚底饼边、中厚饼、薄脆饼边

152
00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:57.240
that's like crispy.
那种很酥脆的。

153
00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:58.960
And people are like, why do you want the thin crust?
然后人们就会问，你为什么非要吃薄脆饼边？

154
00:06:59.060 --> 00:07:00.240
I'm like, give me the cruSt.
我就说，把饼边留给我。

155
00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:01.380
I love the cruSt.
我太爱饼边了。

156
00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:02.980
So that's my garbage.
所以这就是我的怪癖。

157
00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:03.860
What about you, lady?
你呢，女士？

158
00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:04.620
What's your garbage?
你的怪癖是什么？

159
00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:10.180
Well, my garbage is something that I feel like maybe I've shared on the podcast before,
嗯，我的怪癖是那种我觉得我可能在播客里分享过的东西，

160
00:07:10.280 --> 00:07:11.680
but this is what came to mind.
但这就是我脑子里第一个想到的。

161
00:07:11.680 --> 00:07:21.560
It's very Angela Martin of me, but sometimes I get foster kittens and I lick their heads.
这太有安吉拉·马丁的风格了，但有时我带寄养小猫时会舔它们的头。

162
00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:23.080
Like where?
舔哪里？

163
00:07:23.600 --> 00:07:25.080
Between their eyes.
它们的两眼之间。

164
00:07:25.700 --> 00:07:26.980
Like their mama?
像它们的妈妈那样？

165
00:07:27.360 --> 00:07:28.340
Like their mama.
就像它们的妈妈那样。

166
00:07:28.760 --> 00:07:35.500
Like when they first come in and they're like semi-feral and the only way you can hold them
就像它们刚来的时候，有点半野性，你唯一能抱住它们的方法

167
00:07:35.500 --> 00:07:41.040
is to wrap them up like a little burrito and a blanket and then you snug them up real close
就是用毯子把它们像一个小卷饼一样裹起来，然后把它们紧紧地抱在

168
00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:44.400
on your chest, I always pet them right there.
你的胸口，我总是摸它们那个部位。

169
00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:51.620
But sometimes if they're especially scared, I might give a little lick just to try to,
但有时如果它们特别害怕，我可能会轻轻舔一下，只是为了去，

170
00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:55.200
I don't know, create that bond.
我不知道，建立那种羁绊。

171
00:07:56.160 --> 00:08:00.820
You are so much more Angela Martin in this moment than I am.
此时此刻的你比我更像安吉拉·马丁。

172
00:08:00.980 --> 00:08:01.680
I know.
我知道。

173
00:08:01.680 --> 00:08:06.960
I guess my question is when you lick that little part between their eyes,
我想我的问题是，当你舔它们两眼之间的那个小部位时，

174
00:08:06.960 --> 00:08:08.980
do you get hair on your tongue?
你的舌头会沾上猫毛吗？

175
00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:10.880
Are you then like cluck, cluck, cluck?
你会不会然后像这样，呸，呸，呸？

176
00:08:11.060 --> 00:08:12.180
No, you don't.
不，不会的。

177
00:08:12.200 --> 00:08:12.800
No, you don't.
不，真的不会。

178
00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:13.560
You really don't.
真的不会。

179
00:08:13.560 --> 00:08:14.140
It doesn't come off.
毛不会掉下来。

180
00:08:14.260 --> 00:08:15.060
There's nothing there.
什么都没有。

181
00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:19.220
I give it a couple little licks and then I give it a little smooth with the thumb.
我轻轻舔两下，然后用大拇指顺一顺。

182
00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:23.340
You are a very dedicated Kitty Foster parent.
你真是一个尽职尽责的猫咪寄养妈妈。

183
00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:27.600
I hope by the time this podcast comes out, I have none of them in my house anymore.
我希望等这个播客播出的时候，我家里已经没有一只小猫了。

184
00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:28.900
Because they've all been adopted.
因为它们都已经找到了领养家庭。

185
00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:30.920
Because they've all gone to their forever homes.
因为它们都已经去往了永远的家。

186
00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:35.820
But I'll let you know, I've managed to do cat rescue for 20 years without a foster fail.
不过我得告诉你们，我搞了20年的猫咪救援，从来没有发生过寄养失败却自己收养的情况。

187
00:08:35.960 --> 00:08:37.940
So I'm hoping I can keep up my record.
所以我希望我能保持这个纪录。

188
00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:41.140
There's no way you're going to end up adopting one of these.
你绝对不可能最后收养其中一只的。

189
00:08:41.480 --> 00:08:42.160
There's no way.
绝对不可能。

190
00:08:42.320 --> 00:08:46.140
Every single time you have a litter of kittens that you're fostering, you're like, okay,
每次你寄养一窝小猫时，你都会说，好吧，

191
00:08:46.720 --> 00:08:47.500
I'm going to keep one of them.
我要留下一只。

192
00:08:47.600 --> 00:08:49.700
The odds are not in your favor here.
概率对你可不太有利哦。

193
00:08:49.820 --> 00:08:51.380
You are going to end up keeping one of them.
你最后肯定会留下一只的。

194
00:08:51.460 --> 00:08:53.860
This is a terrible BFFing right now.
你现在可真不是个好闺蜜。

195
00:08:54.060 --> 00:08:56.040
You're supposed to be like, don't worry.
你应该说，别担心。

196
00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:58.140
The right person will find them.
合适的人会找到它们的。

197
00:08:58.320 --> 00:08:59.240
No, it's not about that.
不，重点不是这个。

198
00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:00.880
Don't give in to this temptation.
不要向这种诱惑低头。

199
00:09:01.400 --> 00:09:02.920
No, it's not about that.
不，重点不是这个。

200
00:09:02.920 --> 00:09:06.040
Why is it a temptation if you make a connection with one of the kitties?
如果你和其中一只小猫建立起了连接，为什么说这是一种诱惑呢？

201
00:09:06.800 --> 00:09:10.140
Because you can't, then I can't foster another litter of kittens.
因为你做不到，那我以后就不能再寄养一窝小猫了。

202
00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:12.760
Because I can't absorb a kitten every time.
因为我不可能每次都消化掉一只小猫。

203
00:09:13.260 --> 00:09:14.140
I'll be overrun.
我会应接不暇的。

204
00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:15.760
I'm just saying just one time.
我只是说就这么一次。

205
00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:16.920
This is just one time.
这真的只是唯一的一次。

206
00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:17.260
Oh my gosh.
噢，天哪。

207
00:09:17.440 --> 00:09:19.840
You're a rescuer's nightmare right now.
你现在简直是动物救助者的噩梦。

208
00:09:20.220 --> 00:09:21.560
This is not what I need.
这不是我想要的。

209
00:09:22.240 --> 00:09:23.240
I'm sorry, lady.
对不起，女士。

210
00:09:23.600 --> 00:09:24.540
I'm so sorry.
真的很抱歉。

211
00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:25.680
Okay.
好吧。

212
00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:27.540
They're all going to find wonderful homes.
它们都会找到美好的家。

213
00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:28.560
You're doing a great job.
你做得棒极了。

214
00:09:28.700 --> 00:09:29.060
Way to go.
干得好。

215
00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:36.920
So yeah, I guess that's my garbage is that I lick my kittens from time to time.
所以，好吧，我猜我的怪癖就是我偶尔会舔我的小猫。

216
00:09:37.320 --> 00:09:42.080
Like Angela Martin maybe did with her garbage, her literal garbage cat.
就像安吉拉·马丁对她那个字面意义上的垃圾猫做的那样。

217
00:09:42.080 --> 00:09:50.300
I mean, your garbage is coming from such a nurturing place and mine is coming just from like love of bread.
我是说，你的怪癖源于如此关爱，而我的只是源于对面包的热爱。

218
00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:52.880
It's kind of lame.
这有点逊。

219
00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:55.380
Matt, what about your garbage?
马特，你的怪癖是什么？

220
00:09:55.820 --> 00:10:01.120
I think I'm kind of like Angela where I just, it's the eating of other people's leftovers.
我觉得我有点像安吉拉，就是那种喜欢吃别人剩饭的人。

221
00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:02.580
Now hold up, Matt.
等等，马特。

222
00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:05.140
I am not eating other people's leftovers.
我可没吃别人的剩饭。

223
00:10:05.140 --> 00:10:06.740
I just want your pizza cruSt.
我只是想要你的披萨边。

224
00:10:06.880 --> 00:10:10.540
If you and I order a pizza and you're not going to eat your crust, I'll take it.
如果你和我点了一份披萨，而你又不打算吃披萨边，那我就拿走了。

225
00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:11.900
See, I'll take it a step further.
你看，我还要更进一步。

226
00:10:12.120 --> 00:10:15.980
And for me, it's like when my kids come home from school, I open their lunchbox.
对我来说，就像我孩子放学回家时，我打开他们的午餐盒一样。

227
00:10:16.120 --> 00:10:17.560
Especially because it's like around that time of day.
特别是差不多到了一天中的那个时间。

228
00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:18.500
It's like the late afternoon.
就像傍晚时分。

229
00:10:18.740 --> 00:10:19.500
Like I'm kind of hungry.
就像我有点饿了。

230
00:10:19.680 --> 00:10:22.940
I just like, even while I'm still at like the school parking lot, I'll open their little,
我甚至还在学校停车场的时候，就会打开他们的那个，

231
00:10:23.060 --> 00:10:29.100
my little pony lunchbox and grab some warm chicken nuggets and like fruit that's been warmed by the sun.
我的小马宝莉午餐盒，拿几个温热的鸡块，还有被太阳晒温的水果。

232
00:10:29.280 --> 00:10:30.640
It's like a parent's afternoon snack.
这就像是家长的下午茶。

233
00:10:30.640 --> 00:10:31.300
It's a little snack.
这就是个小零食。

234
00:10:31.500 --> 00:10:33.060
Yeah, just my blood sugar is a little low.
对啊，就是我血糖有点低。

235
00:10:33.140 --> 00:10:34.020
I just need a little snack.
我只是需要吃点小零食。

236
00:10:34.220 --> 00:10:35.760
I feel worried for you.
我真为你们感到担心。

237
00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:37.580
I'm worried you're going to get food poisoning.
我担心你们会食物中毒。

238
00:10:37.980 --> 00:10:39.000
So far, so good.
目前为止，一切都好。

239
00:10:39.140 --> 00:10:39.700
Okay, good.
那就好。

240
00:10:40.540 --> 00:10:42.220
But come on, what's in a kid's lunchbox?
但是拜托，孩子的午餐盒里能有什么？

241
00:10:42.360 --> 00:10:42.740
I don't know.
我不知道。

242
00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:44.480
Some goldfish, some pretzels.
一些金鱼饼干，一些蝴蝶脆饼。

243
00:10:44.660 --> 00:10:46.180
So you're getting a soggy pretzel.
所以你吃的是受潮的脆饼。

244
00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:47.220
Yeah, exactly.
对，没错。

245
00:10:47.940 --> 00:10:52.640
Jenna, Matt and I are clearly kind of laid back about food, eating other people's food.
珍娜，我和马特对食物显然都很随性，会吃别人的食物。

246
00:10:53.580 --> 00:10:56.040
Oh, well, thank you so much, Hannah.
哦，好吧，非常感谢，汉娜。

247
00:10:56.380 --> 00:10:58.220
We had fun sharing our garbage.
我们分享各自的怪癖很开心。

248
00:10:58.560 --> 00:11:00.500
And everyone, we're going to take a break.
各位，我们要休息一下。

249
00:11:00.640 --> 00:11:02.020
We'll be back with Joel McHale.
我们将和乔尔·麦克海尔一起回来。

250
00:11:08.600 --> 00:11:11.960
Attention all new and existing members of the WDNC.
请注意所有WDNC的新老会员。

251
00:11:12.200 --> 00:11:15.780
I'm Melanie Sanders, and this is the We Do Not Care Club podcaSt.
我是梅兰妮·桑德斯，这里是“我们不在乎俱乐部”播客节目。

252
00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:20.040
We got to midlife and realized we just simply do not care much anymore.
我们步入中年，然后意识到我们真的再也懒得在乎那么多了。

253
00:11:20.320 --> 00:11:28.140
Now, we got to help each other make sense of hot flashes, itchy ears, chin hair, trifling families, brain fog, and bat wings.
现在，我们要互相帮助，去理清那些潮热、耳朵发痒、下巴长毛、不让人省心的亲戚、脑雾以及拜拜肉。

254
00:11:28.140 --> 00:11:31.000
We are not alone, and we will be heard.
我们并不孤单，我们的声音会被听见。

255
00:11:31.180 --> 00:11:32.900
So come join the WDNC.
所以快来加入WDNC吧。

256
00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:38.280
Follow and listen to the We Do Not Care Club podcast with Melanie Sanders wherever you get your podcaSt.
在各大播客平台搜索并收听由梅兰妮·桑德斯主持的“我们不在乎俱乐部”播客。

257
00:11:42.670 --> 00:11:43.710
Hi, Joel.
嗨，乔尔。

258
00:11:43.990 --> 00:11:45.150
That's our sting, Joel.
那是我们的片头曲，乔尔。

259
00:11:45.430 --> 00:11:46.310
Are you so impressed?
你是不是觉得很震撼？

260
00:11:46.750 --> 00:11:48.850
Can't believe you got sting to do that whole sting.
真不敢相信你竟然把整段片头音乐都放了。

261
00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:49.650
Wow.
哇。

262
00:11:50.150 --> 00:11:51.890
I'm off to a roaring start.
我这可算是一个红红火火的开局。

263
00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:52.490
I apologize.
我道歉。

264
00:11:53.010 --> 00:11:54.170
You stop it.
少来这一套。

265
00:11:54.450 --> 00:11:55.810
Joel, how are you?
乔尔，你最近怎么样？

266
00:11:56.470 --> 00:11:57.170
Look at us.
看看我们。

267
00:11:57.570 --> 00:11:58.130
Drinking.
在喝酒。

268
00:11:58.630 --> 00:11:58.890
Enjoy.
享受吧。

269
00:11:59.150 --> 00:11:59.330
Wait.
等等。

270
00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:00.370
Enjoying ourselves.
我们在享受生活呢。

271
00:12:00.710 --> 00:12:03.330
Remember the last time I stumbled into your podcast?
还记得我上次误打误撞闯进你的播客时吗？

272
00:12:04.170 --> 00:12:05.670
Yes, we do.
当然记得。

273
00:12:05.970 --> 00:12:07.330
That was pre-pandemic, right?
那是大流行爆发前的事了吧？

274
00:12:07.330 --> 00:12:08.250
That was pre-pandemic.
那是大流行爆发前。

275
00:12:08.430 --> 00:12:09.390
That was at Earwolf.
那是在厄尔沃夫公司。

276
00:12:09.390 --> 00:12:15.930
And that's when you could walk down a hallway and kind of look in the sort of sound booth windows and see who was recording.
那时候你可以在走廊里走着，顺便瞅一眼录音棚的窗户，看看是谁在录音。

277
00:12:15.930 --> 00:12:18.790
And you walked by and saw us, and you just came in.
然后你路过看到了我们，就直接进来了。

278
00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:19.870
You're like, hey, guys.
你当时就像是，嘿，伙计们。

279
00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:21.970
You're like, what are you guys doing?
你就像是，你们在干嘛呢？

280
00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:23.630
What's happening here?
这儿发生什么事了？

281
00:12:23.950 --> 00:12:25.250
You guys making a podcast?
你们在录播客吗？

282
00:12:25.950 --> 00:12:30.930
Joel, I have to brag on you a little bit, which is you've got a wicked forehand, my friend.
乔尔，我得好好夸夸你，你的正手击球真的太犀利了，我的朋友。

283
00:12:30.930 --> 00:12:32.550
You've got a really good forehand.
你的正手技术真的很棒。

284
00:12:32.850 --> 00:12:33.570
I'll take that.
那我就却之不恭了。

285
00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:34.650
I had to work on it.
我特意练习过。

286
00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:36.330
You had to work hard on it.
你确实下了苦功去练。

287
00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:38.470
But you've got a really nice forehand.
但你的正手确实很漂亮。

288
00:12:38.470 --> 00:12:43.670
So if you guys ever find yourself in a tennis match with Joel, watch out for the forehand.
所以如果你们有机会和乔尔打网球，可得小心他的正手。

289
00:12:44.090 --> 00:12:45.810
How many times a week do you play, Joel?
乔尔，你一周打几次球？

290
00:12:46.290 --> 00:12:47.730
Every day, almoSt.
几乎每天都打。

291
00:12:48.190 --> 00:12:48.910
Is that right?
是吗？

292
00:12:48.990 --> 00:12:49.110
Yeah.
对。

293
00:12:49.470 --> 00:12:50.410
Do you get out there every day?
你每天都会去打吗？

294
00:12:50.570 --> 00:12:50.770
Yeah.
对。

295
00:12:50.870 --> 00:12:51.910
My son plays.
我儿子也打。

296
00:12:52.010 --> 00:12:54.650
He's 17 and on his high school team.
他17岁了，是高中校队的。

297
00:12:54.710 --> 00:12:57.010
So that really helps.
所以这真的很有帮助。

298
00:12:57.230 --> 00:12:59.310
And we have a tennis court.
而且我们家就有网球场。

299
00:12:59.310 --> 00:13:01.910
Yes, I've done well, everyone.
没错，各位，我混得挺成功的。

300
00:13:02.670 --> 00:13:04.230
I just want to let people know.
我只是想让大家知道这一点。

301
00:13:04.430 --> 00:13:05.550
That's what I spent my money on.
那就是我花钱买的东西。

302
00:13:05.810 --> 00:13:09.610
I will say you share, though, because I do not have a tennis court, but you're like,
不过，我得说你们挺大方的，因为我没有网球场，但你们会说：

303
00:13:09.690 --> 00:13:10.770
Ange, just come over.
安吉，直接过来吧。

304
00:13:11.050 --> 00:13:13.250
And then I come and I show up with homemade granola.
然后我就去了，还带着自制的麦片。

305
00:13:14.070 --> 00:13:15.850
I just leave you guys granola.
我只是把麦片留给你们。

306
00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:17.370
That's our trade.
这就是我们的交易。

307
00:13:17.530 --> 00:13:18.770
Sarah loves that homemade.
萨拉可喜欢这种自制的了。

308
00:13:18.910 --> 00:13:19.110
Oh, my.
天哪。

309
00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:20.690
She won't stop talking about it.
她一直赞不绝口。

310
00:13:20.770 --> 00:13:21.890
How did they do it?
他们是怎么做到的？

311
00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:25.270
It's toasty and it's so flavorful.
它烤得很脆，味道太丰富了。

312
00:13:25.290 --> 00:13:26.990
It's salty and sweet.
又咸又甜。

313
00:13:27.210 --> 00:13:27.730
It's juSt.
简直是。

314
00:13:28.470 --> 00:13:34.590
See, Jenna, you had this whole other world of old people hitting tennis balls and eating granola.
瞧，珍娜，你错过了老年人打网球和吃麦片的世界。

315
00:13:35.670 --> 00:13:38.250
Am I allowed to come over and just eat the granola?
我能过去光吃麦片吗？

316
00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:39.190
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

317
00:13:39.350 --> 00:13:40.750
Is there a place for me?
有我的容身之处吗？

318
00:13:40.930 --> 00:13:41.310
Yes.
有。

319
00:13:41.310 --> 00:13:43.290
We have some benches you can watch from.
我们有长椅，你可以在那儿观看。

320
00:13:43.390 --> 00:13:45.770
Just watch out for the errant line drive.
只要小心飞来的直线球就行。

321
00:13:46.470 --> 00:13:46.670
Yeah.
对。

322
00:13:46.890 --> 00:13:51.110
And a lemon tree that is like the most lemons I've ever seen in my life.
还有一棵柠檬树，那是我这辈子见过结最多柠檬的树。

323
00:13:51.110 --> 00:13:52.350
Right by the tennis court.
就在网球场旁。

324
00:13:52.830 --> 00:13:54.090
Like, it's kind of nuts.
简直有点疯狂。

325
00:13:54.310 --> 00:13:55.750
It is so weighed down.
果实把树枝压得太低了。

326
00:13:55.870 --> 00:13:57.510
It doesn't look like it's going to survive.
感觉它都快撑不下去了。

327
00:13:57.770 --> 00:14:00.870
But then, yeah, there's a, it's a Meyer lemon tree, too.
不过，对，还有一棵，这是一棵梅耶柠檬树。

328
00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:01.630
So it's.
所以它。

329
00:14:02.110 --> 00:14:03.690
Oh, those are the best lemons.
哦，那种柠檬是最好的。

330
00:14:03.890 --> 00:14:05.110
I have a Meyer lemon tree.
我有一棵梅耶柠檬树。

331
00:14:05.390 --> 00:14:06.290
They're sweeter.
它们更甜。

332
00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:07.690
They're so good.
真的很好吃。

333
00:14:08.070 --> 00:14:10.370
And they're growing up in the NorthweSt.
而且它们在西北地区也能生长。

334
00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:11.690
Thank you.
谢谢。

335
00:14:12.070 --> 00:14:13.010
Shout out to Rainn Wilson.
向雷恩·威尔逊致敬。

336
00:14:13.470 --> 00:14:18.090
I never dreamt if you lived in Southern California, you would just plant any, a fruit tree.
我以前做梦也没想到，如果你住在南加州，你只要随便种下一棵果树。

337
00:14:18.090 --> 00:14:21.690
It's going to grow and just start dumping oranges everywhere.
它就会生长，然后到处都是果实。

338
00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:24.250
It seems like Shangri-La when you think about it that way.
这么想的话，感觉就像世外桃源。

339
00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:26.690
Can I ask a question?
我能问个问题吗？

340
00:14:26.830 --> 00:14:28.030
Because I've wondered this.
因为我一直很好奇。

341
00:14:28.150 --> 00:14:32.630
So in my neighborhood, like you said, like living in Southern California, people have fruit
所以在我的社区里，就像你说的，住在南加州，人们都有果

342
00:14:32.630 --> 00:14:32.990
trees.
树。

343
00:14:33.170 --> 00:14:34.130
They just have them.
他们家家都有。

344
00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:41.730
There's pomegranate trees and persimmon trees and so many lemon and lime and orange trees.
有石榴树、柿子树，还有好多柠檬树、青柠树和橘子树。

345
00:14:41.730 --> 00:14:46.970
And you just go for a walk in the neighborhood and sometimes those trees are in people's front
当你走在社区里散步时，有时那些树就在别人的前

346
00:14:46.970 --> 00:14:50.790
yards and they're really full of fruit.
院里，上面挂满了果子。

347
00:14:51.130 --> 00:15:00.450
Do you think it's okay to pick a piece of fruit off of someone else's tree that's in their front
你觉得顺手摘一把别人前院树上的

348
00:15:00.450 --> 00:15:00.870
yard?
果子吃，可以吗？

349
00:15:01.110 --> 00:15:02.270
Are you trespassing?
这算不算私闯民宅？

350
00:15:02.490 --> 00:15:04.330
Are the branches leaning over the fence?
树枝是伸到围栏外面了吗？

351
00:15:04.510 --> 00:15:05.290
There's no fence.
这里没有围栏。

352
00:15:05.290 --> 00:15:14.390
It's just a sidewalk and there's a tree there and maybe you're passing by and you are like,
这只是一条人行道，旁边有一棵树，也许你路过时会想，

353
00:15:14.490 --> 00:15:15.350
I'd love an orange.
我好想吃个橙子。

354
00:15:15.630 --> 00:15:17.290
And there's so many of them.
而且上面有那么多橙子。

355
00:15:17.450 --> 00:15:18.690
There's so many.
有太多了。

356
00:15:19.510 --> 00:15:25.310
So I'll just say, I never do it, but I feel like it should be okay.
所以我要说的是，我从来没这么干过，但我觉得这应该没问题。

357
00:15:25.430 --> 00:15:30.150
As long as you're not taking the last one or there's a dozen left.
只要你不是拿走最后一个，或者还剩下一打的时候。

358
00:15:30.290 --> 00:15:32.430
Like how many oranges does one person need?
话说一个人需要多少个橙子？

359
00:15:32.690 --> 00:15:33.710
I need them all.
我全都要。

360
00:15:33.710 --> 00:15:36.510
Do you not want anyone taking your lemons?
难道你不想让人拿你的柠檬吗？

361
00:15:36.850 --> 00:15:41.230
Well, why do you think we have such a huge wall keeping everyone separated from our lemons?
好吧，你觉得我们为什么要筑起这么高的墙把大家和我们的柠檬隔开？

362
00:15:41.430 --> 00:15:45.670
Well, I have neighbors, guys, and they are side by side, you know, like their driveways
好吧，我有邻居，伙计们，他们的房子紧挨着，你知道，就像他们的车道

363
00:15:45.670 --> 00:15:47.070
line up next to each other.
并排挨在一起。

364
00:15:47.390 --> 00:15:48.470
And on one...
在一边……

365
00:15:48.470 --> 00:15:49.770
That's how it is with my neighbor.
我和我的邻居就是这样。

366
00:15:49.770 --> 00:15:50.030
Okay.
好吧。

367
00:15:50.030 --> 00:15:53.470
So on one side, my neighbor has a lemon tree.
所以在另一边，我的邻居有一棵柠檬树。

368
00:15:53.650 --> 00:15:56.550
It's loaded with lemons and he has just a basket underneath it.
上面挂满了柠檬，树底下就放着一个篮子。

369
00:15:56.630 --> 00:16:00.450
And he's got a little sign that says, please take the lemons, you know, feel free.
他挂了个小牌子上面写着，请拿走这些柠檬，你知道的，别客气。

370
00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:06.530
And then on the other driveway, just a few feet away, another lemon tree loaded with lemons
然后在另一条车道上，仅几英尺远，另一棵柠檬树上也挂满了柠檬

371
00:16:06.530 --> 00:16:08.950
and they have a sign, do not pick the lemons.
他们挂了个牌子，不准采摘柠檬。

372
00:16:09.250 --> 00:16:10.190
So it's like...
所以就像是……

373
00:16:10.190 --> 00:16:10.890
That's not true.
这不是真的。

374
00:16:10.890 --> 00:16:11.690
Are you serious?
你是认真的吗？

375
00:16:11.770 --> 00:16:12.810
It is true.
这是真的。

376
00:16:12.810 --> 00:16:13.550
Oh my God.
哦，天哪。

377
00:16:13.670 --> 00:16:14.410
I promise you.
我向你保证。

378
00:16:14.470 --> 00:16:15.430
And I'm like, what?
当时我就想，什么？

379
00:16:15.610 --> 00:16:16.050
These are...
这些是……

380
00:16:16.050 --> 00:16:17.870
These two people have very different philosophies.
这两个人的生活哲学完全不同。

381
00:16:17.990 --> 00:16:19.530
They're letting the whole neighborhood know about it.
他们正让整个社区都知道这件事。

382
00:16:19.830 --> 00:16:19.990
Yeah.
是啊。

383
00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:20.510
All right.
好吧。

384
00:16:20.690 --> 00:16:24.190
Well, on those good vibes, I think it's time.
带着这种美好的氛围，我觉得是时候了。

385
00:16:24.470 --> 00:16:27.270
You try to transition to this game, Angela?
安吉拉，你想试着过渡到这个游戏吗？

386
00:16:27.910 --> 00:16:28.750
I'm trying.
我在试。

387
00:16:28.970 --> 00:16:29.350
I think she is.
我觉得她在试。

388
00:16:29.470 --> 00:16:30.590
Joel, I'm trying.
乔尔，我在努力。

389
00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:32.590
You should know this about me.
关于我，你应该知道这一点。

390
00:16:32.670 --> 00:16:34.970
I'm horrible at transitions and segues.
我不擅长话题转换和过渡。

391
00:16:35.270 --> 00:16:38.590
Like if we're at a cocktail party and I really want to talk to you and you're talking to people
比如我们在鸡尾酒会上，我真的很想跟你说话，而你正在跟别人聊天

392
00:16:38.590 --> 00:16:43.750
and like you're standing, let's say, by a Christmas tree, I might walk up and be like,
比如你站着，比方说，在一棵圣诞树旁，我可能会走过去说，

393
00:16:44.910 --> 00:16:47.170
here's the thing about Christmas trees.
事情是这样的，关于圣诞树。

394
00:16:47.450 --> 00:16:48.850
Like the whole...
就像整个……

395
00:16:50.090 --> 00:16:51.330
The whole energy.
整个气场。

396
00:16:51.550 --> 00:16:55.090
That sounds like a segue into conversation though.
听起来倒像是切入对话的过渡。

397
00:16:55.210 --> 00:16:55.410
Yeah.
是啊。

398
00:16:55.490 --> 00:16:59.770
I mean, if you were to launch into like, the Atlas Mountains are in Morocco.
我的意思是，如果你突然抛出一句，阿特拉斯山脉在摩洛哥。

399
00:17:00.130 --> 00:17:00.690
I'm like, what?
我会想，什么？

400
00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:02.050
Yeah.
是啊。

401
00:17:02.050 --> 00:17:05.170
No, I just look at something right in front of me and comment.
不，我只是看着眼前的某样东西然后发表评论。

402
00:17:05.730 --> 00:17:06.170
Okay.
好的。

403
00:17:06.290 --> 00:17:10.150
This is going to be the best transition of your whole effing life.
这将是你这辈子的绝妙过渡。

404
00:17:10.310 --> 00:17:10.790
Are you ready?
准备好了吗？

405
00:17:11.030 --> 00:17:12.530
Now there's a lot of pressure here.
现在这儿压力可大了。

406
00:17:12.610 --> 00:17:16.430
You know who's so much fun at a party and who's great at playing games?
你知道谁在派对上最好玩、谁最擅长玩游戏吗？

407
00:17:16.430 --> 00:17:18.590
It's our dear friend, Joel McHale.
是我们亲爱的朋友，乔尔·麦克海尔。

408
00:17:18.750 --> 00:17:23.670
And we thought, who better than to play two truths and one lie with?
我们觉得，还有谁比他更适合玩“两真一假”呢？

409
00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:25.390
We had Creed Bratton on.
我们曾请来克里德·布拉顿。

410
00:17:25.650 --> 00:17:26.550
He played it.
他玩了这个游戏。

411
00:17:26.670 --> 00:17:28.010
Joel, no pressure.
乔尔，别有压力。

412
00:17:28.270 --> 00:17:30.570
He is amazing at two truths and a lie.
他玩“两真一假”超级厉害。

413
00:17:30.570 --> 00:17:32.830
At lying and telling the truth.
在撒谎和说实话这方面。

414
00:17:33.130 --> 00:17:33.390
Uh-huh.
嗯哼。

415
00:17:33.490 --> 00:17:36.550
Because his truths and his lies are kind of blurry.
因为他的真话和谎言有点扑朔迷离。

416
00:17:37.230 --> 00:17:39.590
And what we're going to need from you...
所以我们需要你做的是……

417
00:17:39.590 --> 00:17:41.770
Jenna and I did not do a lot of Googling on you.
珍娜和我并没有在谷歌上搜你太多资料。

418
00:17:41.890 --> 00:17:43.450
We wanted to be surprised here.
我们想在这里感到惊喜。

419
00:17:43.570 --> 00:17:46.010
We don't want to know all your ins and outs, okay?
我们不想了解你的全部底细，好吗？

420
00:17:46.130 --> 00:17:46.890
All your business.
你所有的私事。

421
00:17:47.570 --> 00:17:52.830
So we're going to need you to tell us two truths and a lie in any order.
所以我们需要你按任意顺序告诉我们两个真事和一个谎言。

422
00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:57.830
And then Jenna and I are going to guess which one is the lie.
然后珍娜和我来猜哪一个是谎言。

423
00:17:57.830 --> 00:18:01.030
And you folks listening out there can play along with us.
在听节目的各位也可以和我们一起玩。

424
00:18:01.590 --> 00:18:02.750
So, Joel, you're up.
所以，乔尔，轮到你了。

425
00:18:02.930 --> 00:18:06.090
You have to tell us now two truths and a lie.
你现在必须告诉我们两个真事和一个谎言。

426
00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:07.470
And it can be anything.
什么都可以。

427
00:18:08.190 --> 00:18:09.650
It can be anything.
什么都可以。

428
00:18:11.110 --> 00:18:13.910
So it could be like, I could tell a 25-minute story.
所以就像，我可以讲一个25分钟的故事。

429
00:18:15.510 --> 00:18:15.950
Sure.
当然。

430
00:18:16.270 --> 00:18:16.430
Sure.
当然。

431
00:18:17.270 --> 00:18:18.830
Three 25-minute stories.
三个25分钟的故事。

432
00:18:19.090 --> 00:18:21.470
But you are going to have to take a break.
但你得休息一下。

433
00:18:21.530 --> 00:18:22.390
And one of them's a lie.
其中一个是谎言。

434
00:18:22.530 --> 00:18:26.950
You will have to pause because I'm going to have to go pee if you do three 25-minute stories.
你得暂停一下，因为如果你讲三个25分钟的故事，我要去上厕所。

435
00:18:26.950 --> 00:18:31.190
I will be offended because these stories are real humdingers.
我会生气的，因为这些故事可都是精彩绝伦的奇事。

436
00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:31.970
Okay.
好的。

437
00:18:32.330 --> 00:18:34.010
Two truths and a lie with Joel McHale.
与乔尔·麦克海尔一起玩“两真一假”。

438
00:18:34.130 --> 00:18:34.510
Here we go.
我们开始吧。

439
00:18:34.770 --> 00:18:38.450
Two truths and a lie.
两真一假。

440
00:18:38.730 --> 00:18:39.530
Here we go.
我们开始吧。

441
00:18:40.610 --> 00:18:43.210
I have been bitten by a bear.
我曾被熊咬过。

442
00:18:43.850 --> 00:18:49.110
I have met Luciano Pavarotti when he was alive, obviously.
我见过卢西亚诺·帕瓦罗蒂，当然是他活着的时候。

443
00:18:49.410 --> 00:18:50.450
I didn't meet him after he died.
我没在他死后见过他。

444
00:18:51.470 --> 00:18:53.990
And I quit drinking scotch.
我戒了苏格兰威士忌。

445
00:18:55.980 --> 00:18:56.520
Okay.
好吧。

446
00:18:56.520 --> 00:18:56.660
Okay.
好的。

447
00:18:59.050 --> 00:19:00.030
Two truths and a lie.
两真一假。

448
00:19:00.470 --> 00:19:01.430
Oh, is it two truths?
哦，是两个真事吗？

449
00:19:02.030 --> 00:19:03.690
Two truths and a lie.
两真一假。

450
00:19:04.430 --> 00:19:07.010
Did you just give us two lies and one truth?
你刚才是不是给了我们两个谎言和一个真事？

451
00:19:07.370 --> 00:19:07.990
Did you really?
真的吗？

452
00:19:08.310 --> 00:19:09.090
Yeah, let's do that.
好啊，就这么办。

453
00:19:09.210 --> 00:19:09.410
Okay.
行。

454
00:19:09.490 --> 00:19:12.250
We're now playing two lies and one truth.
我们现在来玩“两假一真”。

455
00:19:12.610 --> 00:19:13.050
I like that.
我喜欢这个。

456
00:19:13.290 --> 00:19:13.830
With Joel McHale.
有请乔尔·麦克海尔。

457
00:19:14.330 --> 00:19:22.410
I just saw you at a holiday party where I believe you were drinking scotch.
我刚在一次节日派对上看见你，当时我深信你在喝苏格兰威士忌。

458
00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:27.990
And so I am asking myself, how recently did you stop drinking scotch?
所以我一直在问自己，你究竟是什么时候戒掉苏格兰威士忌的？

459
00:19:28.130 --> 00:19:29.690
Were you not drinking scotch at that party?
你当时在那个派对上没喝苏格兰威士忌吗？

460
00:19:29.690 --> 00:19:29.890
I was not drinking scotch at that party.
我当时在那个派对上没喝苏格兰威士忌。

461
00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:31.370
Were you not drinking an old-fashioned?
你当时没在喝老式鸡尾酒吗？

462
00:19:32.750 --> 00:19:33.510
You weren't?
没有吗？

463
00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:34.950
I was drinking sparkling wine.
我在喝起泡酒。

464
00:19:35.110 --> 00:19:36.030
Sparkling wine?
起泡酒？

465
00:19:36.030 --> 00:19:37.470
You know, it wasn't a champagne.
你知道的，那不是香槟。

466
00:19:37.670 --> 00:19:38.750
It was a prosecco.
那是普洛赛克。

467
00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:40.310
It was prosecco.
那是普洛赛克。

468
00:19:40.470 --> 00:19:41.070
You were?
是吗？

469
00:19:41.270 --> 00:19:45.130
I was definitely not drinking an old-fashioned.
我绝对没有在喝老式鸡尾酒。

470
00:19:46.110 --> 00:19:46.670
Okay.
好吧。

471
00:19:47.030 --> 00:19:52.490
I think in my entire lifetime, I have had maybe two old-fashions.
我想在我的一生中，大概只喝过两次老式鸡尾酒。

472
00:19:53.230 --> 00:19:53.790
Wow.
哇。

473
00:19:54.310 --> 00:19:55.570
Jenna, you love an old-fashioned.
珍娜，你最爱老式鸡尾酒了。

474
00:19:56.710 --> 00:19:58.990
Maybe you were drinking the old-fashioned.
也许当时喝老式鸡尾酒的是你。

