00:26:13.000 --> 00:26:15.760
Don't make a weird, awkward transition into the conversation.
别让谈话的过渡显得怪异又尴尬。

650
00:26:16.420 --> 00:26:17.620
Do you have any lemons?
你有柠檬吗？

651
00:26:18.780 --> 00:26:19.260
What?
什么？

652
00:26:19.900 --> 00:26:21.880
Fancy finding you buy some lemons.
居然能在你这儿买到柠檬。

653
00:26:22.240 --> 00:26:24.960
Angela Kinsey's trying to steal lemons from us.
安吉拉·金西正试图从我们这儿偷柠檬。

654
00:26:25.100 --> 00:26:27.320
Are we ever going to hear about this bear attack?
我们到底还能不能听到那个熊袭击的故事了？

655
00:26:27.780 --> 00:26:29.080
What do I need to do?
我需要做什么？

656
00:26:29.200 --> 00:26:31.500
I need to hear the story of the bear attack.
我想听听熊袭击的故事。

657
00:26:31.700 --> 00:26:37.980
It was for a show called The Great Indoors, which was on CBS for one season in 2016.
那是为了一个叫《室内奇兵》的节目，2016年在CBS播了一季。

658
00:26:37.980 --> 00:26:47.000
It was me, the great Stephen Fry, Chris Mintz, Plass, Christine Coe, Deborah Baker Jr., and Sean Brown.
有我、伟大的斯蒂芬·弗雷、克里斯·明茨-普拉斯、克里斯蒂娜·科e、黛博拉·贝克·Jr.和肖恩·布朗。

659
00:26:47.700 --> 00:26:50.140
And Stephen Fry and I, he played my boss.
我和斯蒂芬·弗雷搭档，他演我的老板。

660
00:26:50.660 --> 00:26:53.640
Anyway, we did this scene with a bear cub.
总之，我们拍了一场有小熊的戏。

661
00:26:53.640 --> 00:27:04.960
I had to hold the bear cub while I gave a speech and they were like, okay, so the bear will probably become impatient.
我得抱着小熊做演讲，他们跟我说，好吧，这只熊可能会变得没有耐心。

662
00:27:04.960 --> 00:27:10.040
You got about 40 seconds because the bear doesn't really like to be held.
你大概只有40秒时间，因为熊其实不喜欢被人抱着。

663
00:27:10.040 --> 00:27:13.240
And so you're holding the bear and the bear's cuddly.
你抱着熊，熊感觉挺可爱的。

664
00:27:13.240 --> 00:27:14.260
It's a bear cub.
它是一只小熊。

665
00:27:14.440 --> 00:27:16.100
It weighs 50 pounds.
它有50磅重。

666
00:27:16.640 --> 00:27:20.160
And you're holding this bear and I start giving the speech as fast as I can.
你抱着这只熊，我开始以最快的速度发表讲演。

667
00:27:20.500 --> 00:27:22.860
And then they were like, he'll just be annoyed.
然后他们说，它只会觉得烦躁。

668
00:27:22.980 --> 00:27:26.960
And he might bite you just to test things out.
它可能会咬你一口来试探试探。

669
00:27:26.960 --> 00:27:33.260
So I was wearing like three layers and that thing bit me in the arm and that thing, that beautiful thing.
所以我穿了大约三层衣服，那家伙一口咬在我的胳膊上，那个家伙，那个美丽的家伙。

670
00:27:33.560 --> 00:27:35.860
And so bears do not have sharp teeth.
而且熊的牙齿并不锋利。

671
00:27:36.180 --> 00:27:38.920
They have teeth that crush things.
它们的牙齿是用来咬碎东西的。

672
00:27:39.120 --> 00:27:39.840
Oh no!
哦，不！

673
00:27:40.480 --> 00:27:41.740
Not like a puppy at all.
一点也不像小狗。

674
00:27:41.840 --> 00:27:46.160
It just squeezes so hard because it's like they crush bones with them.
它只是咬得特别紧，因为它们的牙齿是用来咬碎骨头的。

675
00:27:46.580 --> 00:27:53.200
So it didn't break skin, but it left this gigantic mouth-shaped bruise on my arm.
所以它没咬破皮肤，但在我胳膊上留下了这个巨大的、嘴巴形状的淤青。

676
00:27:53.760 --> 00:27:56.960
So then I dropped the bear out of pain.
然后我疼得把熊给扔了。

677
00:27:57.420 --> 00:28:03.000
And the bear didn't, the guy was like, oh yeah, the bear falls out of trees all the time, like three feet.
熊没怎么样，驯兽师说，哦对，熊经常从树上掉下来，大概三英尺高。

678
00:28:03.140 --> 00:28:05.460
You can't, he was like, this is nothing.
你不能，他说，这不算什么。

679
00:28:05.640 --> 00:28:07.020
He's never been happier.
它从来没这么开心过。

680
00:28:07.220 --> 00:28:09.880
And then Stephen Fry had to pick him up and hold him and give a speech.
然后斯蒂芬·弗雷不得不把它抱起来，抱着它做演讲。

681
00:28:10.020 --> 00:28:11.580
And the exact same thing happened.
结果完全一样。

682
00:28:13.000 --> 00:28:13.760
So anyway.
所以总之。

683
00:28:14.040 --> 00:28:15.840
Was it just the one take though?
不过只拍了一条吗？

684
00:28:16.060 --> 00:28:17.480
They weren't like, can you go again?
他们没有说，能再来一条吗？

685
00:28:17.620 --> 00:28:18.400
We did one take.
我们就拍了一条。

686
00:28:18.620 --> 00:28:20.560
And they were, yeah, that was compared.
他们说，对，那就算过了。

687
00:28:20.560 --> 00:28:23.420
They had river otters on set at one point.
他们有一次在片场弄了些河獭。

688
00:28:23.540 --> 00:28:25.040
They wanted me to hold a river otter.
他们想让我抱一只河獭。

689
00:28:25.220 --> 00:28:30.900
And that was about 20 times more terrifying because they are big and they move so faSt.
那要吓人大约20倍，因为它们个头很大，而且动得太快了。

690
00:28:31.080 --> 00:28:35.580
And they were eating raw chicken and crushing the bones in their teeth.
它们在吃生鸡肉，用牙齿把骨头咬得粉碎。

691
00:28:35.800 --> 00:28:37.920
Just, just like it's popcorn.
就，就像吃爆米花一样。

692
00:28:38.300 --> 00:28:41.700
And I'm like, the bear was just mellow and cool.
而我觉得，那只熊其实很温顺很酷。

693
00:28:42.080 --> 00:28:45.580
And the bear on the ground, just walking around was like a nice dog.
那只在地上走来走去的熊就像一只好狗狗。

694
00:28:45.800 --> 00:28:47.740
You know, I actually have a bear story.
你知道的，我其实也有个关于熊的故事。

695
00:28:47.740 --> 00:28:48.000
Oh!
哦！

696
00:28:48.340 --> 00:28:49.280
If you're interested.
如果你感兴趣的话。

697
00:28:49.920 --> 00:28:58.680
Okay, so I'm not sure if I've told this story on our podcast before, but early in the office shoot, I think maybe I've mentioned it.
好吧，我不确定我以前在我们的播客里有没有讲过这个故事，但在《办公室》拍摄的早期，我想我可能提过。

698
00:28:59.060 --> 00:29:02.980
They asked me and John and Rain to do a photo shoot.
他们让我、约翰和雷恩去拍一组照片。

699
00:29:03.120 --> 00:29:04.800
I think it was for TV Guide.
我想那是为《电视指南》拍的。

700
00:29:05.340 --> 00:29:13.160
And for a reason I don't know, it was the three of us and a fully grown bear, like a full bear.
由于我不知道的原因，当时是我们三个加上一只完全长大的熊，就像一头真正的熊。

701
00:29:13.960 --> 00:29:17.160
And the bear was coming through the window.
然后那头熊就从窗户闯了进来。

702
00:29:17.460 --> 00:29:17.900
What?
什么？

703
00:29:18.100 --> 00:29:20.120
And then the three of us were like, ah!
然后我们三个当时就：啊！

704
00:29:20.760 --> 00:29:22.840
And I have no memory of this lady.
而且我对这位女士完全没有记忆。

705
00:29:22.940 --> 00:29:27.600
You can Google it and I think you can find the image of us with this bear.
你可以在谷歌上搜一下，我觉得你能找到我们和这头熊的合影。

706
00:29:27.600 --> 00:29:31.800
And so they were kind of setting it up and we were getting ready to go.
当时他们正在布景，我们也准备要开始了。

707
00:29:32.020 --> 00:29:33.980
And then someone came in and said, you know what?
然后有人进来，说你知道吗？

708
00:29:34.080 --> 00:29:36.480
We've decided we're going to do these separate.
我们决定把这些分开拍。

709
00:29:36.800 --> 00:29:45.560
So you guys just react as if the bear is there and then we'll bring the bear out later and we'll get the shot of the bear and we'll put them together.
所以你们就先做出熊在现场的反应，然后我们稍后把熊带出来，拍下熊的镜头，再把它们剪辑到一起。

710
00:29:45.560 --> 00:29:47.260
And we were like, that sounds good.
当时我们就觉得，听起来不错。

711
00:29:47.540 --> 00:29:48.980
I kid you not.
我真的没骗你。

712
00:29:49.560 --> 00:29:54.100
A couple years later, I am pretty sure this is true.
几年后，我非常确定这是真的。

713
00:29:54.400 --> 00:30:01.160
I don't want to disparage this bear if I'm wrong, but I think he killed his trainer.
如果我记错了，我可不想贬低这头熊，但我觉得它把训练员给杀了。

714
00:30:01.600 --> 00:30:03.080
Oh my gosh.
我的天哪。

715
00:30:03.280 --> 00:30:03.720
I mean.
我是说。

716
00:30:03.920 --> 00:30:05.260
I think he killed someone.
我觉得它杀了个人。

717
00:30:05.600 --> 00:30:08.380
When you have a gigantic wild animal.
当你养了一只巨大的野生动物时。

718
00:30:09.580 --> 00:30:23.920
Yeah, and so I'm so grateful that on the day they decided to shoot us separately because it turns out this bear, he had worked a long time and I think he was done.
对啊，所以我特别庆幸他们那天决定让我们分开拍，因为后来证明这头熊，它工作了很长时间，我觉得它受够了。

719
00:30:24.140 --> 00:30:25.240
He was grumpy.
它脾气很暴躁。

720
00:30:25.540 --> 00:30:27.060
He wasn't into it anymore.
它再也不想配合了。

721
00:30:27.060 --> 00:30:29.220
He didn't want to be a performing bear.
它不想当一头表演熊了。

722
00:30:29.480 --> 00:30:33.440
That bear may not even had intended to kill his trainer.
那头熊甚至可能不是故意要杀它的训练员的。

723
00:30:33.980 --> 00:30:34.580
Right.
对。

724
00:30:34.580 --> 00:30:42.040
It could have just been like, hey, and they just happened to have, you know, their arm is a thousand times more powerful than a human arm.
可能只是想说，嘿，而且他们的力气，你知道的，它们的胳膊比人类的胳膊强壮成千上万倍。

725
00:30:42.240 --> 00:30:42.440
So then.
所以呢。

726
00:30:42.660 --> 00:30:42.820
Right.
没错。

727
00:30:43.520 --> 00:30:55.180
I did a shoot with some monkeys, some chimpanzees, and I got there and it's for a magazine and they were like, so don't look the monkeys in the eye.
我曾经和一些猴子、一些黑猩猩合作拍过照，我到了现场，那是为一家杂志拍的，他们就说，千万不要直视猴子的眼睛。

728
00:30:55.540 --> 00:30:56.240
No, don't.
千万别。

729
00:30:56.460 --> 00:30:58.720
And then I said, that's the rule.
然后我说，这就是规矩。

730
00:30:58.720 --> 00:31:10.640
Then I, yeah, then I literally was like, you shoot those guys separately because I, I'm not going to accidentally gaze at this thing and then it's going to come at me and kill me.
然后我，对，我当时真的说：你们把那些家伙分开拍，因为我可不想不小心盯着这东西看，然后它就扑过来把我给杀了。

731
00:31:10.800 --> 00:31:14.620
Also, now you've told me, don't look at the monkey in the eye and that's all I'm going to do.
而且，既然你现在告诉了我“别直视猴子的眼睛”，那我满脑子就只想这么干了。

732
00:31:15.000 --> 00:31:16.500
So that's what's in my brain now.
所以这就是我脑子里现在想的事。

733
00:31:16.580 --> 00:31:17.320
Got to look him in the eye.
非得直视它的眼睛不可。

734
00:31:17.440 --> 00:31:18.360
I got to see what happens.
我得看看会发生什么。

735
00:31:19.060 --> 00:31:26.940
Julie, it seems like you've done a lot of television programs with animals because you are now in season four of animal control.
茱莉，听起来你参加过很多有动物参与的电视节目，因为你现在正在拍《动物控制》第四季。

736
00:31:26.940 --> 00:31:35.120
I don't know how that worked out, but yeah, I worked with a ton of animals and I don't know how it all happened.
我不知道这是怎么做到的，不过对，我合作过大量的动物，我也不知道这一切是怎么发生的。

737
00:31:35.300 --> 00:31:36.000
I do love them.
我确实很爱它们。

738
00:31:36.380 --> 00:31:37.800
I love them to death.
我爱死它们了。

739
00:31:37.960 --> 00:31:43.380
Like I got to ride a camel this year down a residential street in Vancouver and I was like, this is the greateSt.
比如今年我在温哥华的一条住宅区街道上骑了骆驼，当时我就想，这太棒了。

740
00:31:43.940 --> 00:31:45.240
Can't believe this has happened.
真不敢相信这居然发生了。

741
00:31:45.360 --> 00:31:46.860
I have a question for you.
我有个问题想问你。

742
00:31:48.000 --> 00:31:50.900
Season four, episode one, animal control.
第四季第一集，《动物控制》。

743
00:31:51.140 --> 00:31:51.980
There's a horse.
有一匹马。

744
00:31:52.020 --> 00:31:53.540
It's going down the road.
它在路上跑着。

745
00:31:54.340 --> 00:32:03.820
You jump out of a moving car, a slow moving car, and you kind of roll and then you jog up to the horse and you mount it.
你从一辆移动的车里跳出来，一辆缓慢移动的车，然后你顺势一滚，接着小跑着靠近那匹马并翻身上去。

746
00:32:04.080 --> 00:32:05.560
Yes, that was not me.
对，那不是我。

747
00:32:06.040 --> 00:32:08.000
But did you fall out of the car?
但你是从车里摔出来的吗？

748
00:32:08.220 --> 00:32:16.180
Because I believe you rolled out of the car, but I'm like, I think the guy mounting the horse was not you because it's on your back.
因为我觉得你是从车里滚出来的，但我想，上马的那个人应该不是你，因为那是拍你的背影。

749
00:32:16.320 --> 00:32:19.420
And then we go to the front of you and you are on the horse.
然后镜头转到你的正面，你已经在马上了。

750
00:32:19.420 --> 00:32:23.280
Yes, but I just, what an opener, what a season opener.
对，不过我只想说，这开场太棒了，真是一个绝佳的季度首播。

751
00:32:23.600 --> 00:32:27.980
Yeah, we shut down a highway in Vancouver and we had like six hours total.
对，我们在温哥华封了一条高速公路，总共只有大约六个小时的时间。

752
00:32:28.660 --> 00:32:34.800
So we ran out there and got everything all set up and got in and got out and it worked.
所以我们跑过去把一切都布置好，进去又出来，而且成功了。

753
00:32:34.940 --> 00:32:44.240
So they would not let me fall out of the truck, even though I'm one of those guys that believes I can prove that I'm going to live forever through physical accomplishments.
所以他们不让我从卡车上掉下去，尽管我是那种觉得自己能通过体能成就证明自己长生不老的人。

754
00:32:44.740 --> 00:32:48.220
So they were like, that's exactly why we're not allowing you to roll out of the truck.
所以他们就像是在说，这正是我们不准你从卡车上滚下来的原因。

755
00:32:48.340 --> 00:32:49.560
So I had a bunch of pads on.
所以我身上绑了一堆垫子。

756
00:32:49.660 --> 00:32:51.620
So I did the last final roll.
于是我做了最后一次翻滚。

757
00:32:51.980 --> 00:32:52.220
Okay.
好吧。

758
00:32:52.480 --> 00:32:57.700
The only thing scary about that is there was a team of trucks all driving and they all had to be at a certain speed.
唯一吓人的地方是有一队卡车都在开，而且它们都必须保持特定的速度。

759
00:32:57.840 --> 00:33:00.880
So they're like, make sure you get up fast or you're going to get hit by this truck.
所以他们会说，确保你赶快爬起来，否则你会被这辆卡车撞到。

760
00:33:01.220 --> 00:33:02.040
Oh my gosh.
噢天哪。

761
00:33:02.460 --> 00:33:02.640
Great.
太棒了。

762
00:33:02.640 --> 00:33:12.460
And then the guy that did the horse thing, that jump, I mean, I could not have done that jump because he grabbed the pommel and then he just flipped his legs up.
还有那个做马术动作的家伙，那个跳跃，我是说，我根本做不出那种跳跃，因为他抓住鞍把，然后双腿一甩。

763
00:33:12.560 --> 00:33:17.800
And he, that dude is one of the greatest like horse trainers and performers on the planet.
而且他，那家伙是地球上最伟大的训马师和表演者之一。

764
00:33:18.040 --> 00:33:20.460
It was like an old timey mounting of a horse.
那就像是一种老式的上马方式。

765
00:33:20.460 --> 00:33:28.740
It was like in ye olde west, how you might like run out into the field and just jump on the back of the horse.
就像在古老的西部，你可能会跑进田野里直接跳到马背上一样。

766
00:33:28.940 --> 00:33:29.540
It was very cool.
真的很酷。

767
00:33:29.700 --> 00:33:30.300
Thank you.
谢谢你。

768
00:33:32.700 --> 00:33:37.700
For this season, because now the two animal control units have merged.
对于这一季，因为现在两个动物管理小组合并了。

769
00:33:38.420 --> 00:33:41.060
Is that going to be the main crux of the season?
这会是这一季的核心关键吗？

770
00:33:41.340 --> 00:33:42.980
That is the main crux of the season.
这确实是这一季的核心关键。

771
00:33:44.420 --> 00:33:46.120
And everybody dies.
然后所有人都死了。

772
00:33:46.860 --> 00:33:47.780
Stop it.
别闹了。

773
00:33:48.080 --> 00:33:48.920
Stop it.
住手。

774
00:33:49.080 --> 00:33:50.420
What happens in season five?
第五季会发生什么？

775
00:33:50.420 --> 00:33:54.740
I don't know if you've seen Hamlet or the movie Hamnet.
我不知道你有没有看过《哈姆雷特》或者电影《哈姆内特》。

776
00:33:55.760 --> 00:33:56.320
Okay.
好吧。

777
00:33:56.760 --> 00:33:58.660
But yeah, there's a duel at the end.
但对，结尾处有一场决斗。

778
00:33:58.840 --> 00:34:01.720
One of us is poisoned and then accidentally poisons the other.
我们其中一人中毒了，然后又阴差阳错地毒死了另一个人。

779
00:34:01.720 --> 00:34:03.120
And that's it.
就这样。

780
00:34:03.500 --> 00:34:04.120
That's it.
就这样。

781
00:34:04.220 --> 00:34:07.080
It's like Hamlet and Red Wedding all at once.
这简直就像《哈姆雷特》和血色婚礼的结合体。

782
00:34:07.440 --> 00:34:09.660
Oh, the Red Wedding, which I want Jenna to watch.
噢，血色婚礼，我很想让珍娜看看。

783
00:34:09.840 --> 00:34:17.640
I don't know why I find this hard to believe, but I feel like Fox is not letting the show end that way this year.
我不知道为什么我觉得这很难置信，但我觉得福克斯今年不会让节目以这种方式结束。

784
00:34:17.640 --> 00:34:24.980
I mean, Kyla Pratt and Jerry Dee, who came onto the show, and boy, just knocking it out of the park.
我是说，凯拉·普拉特和杰里·迪伊加入这部剧后，天哪，简直表现得太出色了。

785
00:34:25.220 --> 00:34:29.520
Just so funny and just wonderful nemesis.
就是超级搞笑，而且是非常棒的死对头。

786
00:34:29.840 --> 00:34:31.600
Yeah, it's good times.
对，那是一段美好的时光。

787
00:34:31.800 --> 00:34:32.760
It's Aaron now.
现在是亚伦了。

788
00:34:32.760 --> 00:34:36.040
I think we're almost to the season closer.
我想我们快到季终集了。

789
00:34:36.480 --> 00:34:43.580
And I do want to say this, you guys, that for folks that love The Office, some of my favorite scenes, Joel,
我真的很想说，各位，对于喜欢《办公室》的剧迷来说，我最喜欢的一些场景，乔尔，

790
00:34:43.580 --> 00:34:46.820
are when y'all are just all in The Office just giving each other a bunch of crap.
就是当你们所有人都在办公室里互相开玩笑、斗嘴的时候。

791
00:34:46.820 --> 00:34:54.320
You know, like the animal control actual offices with the desks and the whole sort of vibe reminded me a lot of us in the bullpen of The Office.
你知道的，就像动物管理部门真正的办公室，有办公桌和那种整体氛围，让我非常想起我们在《办公室》开放式办公区的时候。

792
00:34:54.640 --> 00:34:57.880
So, Office fans, you want to check this show out.
所以，《办公室》的粉丝们，你们一定要来看看这部剧。

793
00:34:58.200 --> 00:35:00.600
We literally said this should be like The Office.
我们当时简直直说这应该拍得像《办公室》一样。

794
00:35:00.780 --> 00:35:03.640
It's the interpersonal relationships that all these guys have.
关键在于这群人之间的这种人际关系。

795
00:35:04.000 --> 00:35:07.900
And just keep zipping around those, and we should be okay.
只要围绕这些不断推进，我们应该就没问题。

796
00:35:08.200 --> 00:35:09.120
I'm going to give you this.
这个送给你。

797
00:35:09.120 --> 00:35:12.740
I think it's as if The Office and Brooklyn Nine-Nine had a baby.
我觉得这就好像是《办公室》和《神烦警探》生了个孩子。

798
00:35:13.480 --> 00:35:22.160
Now I feel like you're lying to me because I can't take a compliment, and my imposter syndrome goes to the roof.
现在我觉得你在骗我，因为我承受不起夸奖，我的冒名顶替综合征直接飙升到顶点。

799
00:35:22.640 --> 00:35:27.360
And to even be compared to those shows, it seems insane.
而且能与那些剧集相提并论，简直太疯狂了。

800
00:35:27.360 --> 00:35:29.260
So, I'll take that.
所以，这份赞美我收下了。

801
00:35:29.400 --> 00:35:31.880
Well, it's a ton of fun, and you guys are hilarious.
嗯，这真的太有意思了，而且你们都太逗了。

802
00:35:32.240 --> 00:35:35.520
And I love, like, just shooting the s*** with you, Joel.
我也很喜欢跟你随便闲聊，乔尔。

803
00:35:35.660 --> 00:35:37.120
You're such a just good person.
你真的是个很好的人。

804
00:35:38.200 --> 00:35:39.060
We're so lucky.
我们太幸运了。

805
00:35:39.700 --> 00:35:39.900
Yeah.
是啊。

806
00:35:40.580 --> 00:35:41.980
Joel, thank you so much.
乔尔，非常感谢你。

807
00:35:42.140 --> 00:35:43.680
I just adore you, and I appreciate you.
我真的很崇拜你，也很感激你。

808
00:35:43.940 --> 00:35:46.560
Well, come back on over and play some more tennis.
好啦，随时再过来一起打网球吧。

809
00:35:46.840 --> 00:35:48.740
Jenny, you're welcome to come anytime.
珍妮，你随时都可以来。

810
00:35:49.500 --> 00:35:50.060
Thank you.
谢谢你。

811
00:35:50.180 --> 00:35:51.820
I'll be there to eat the granola.
我会去吃麦片脆饼的。

812
00:35:52.240 --> 00:35:57.840
And everyone else, we're going to take a break, and we're going to be back with Around the Town and The Office Question of the Week.
至于其他人，我们要休息一下，一会儿将带回《走遍小镇》和《本周办公室问答》。

813
00:35:58.080 --> 00:35:58.400
All right.
好的。

814
00:35:58.560 --> 00:35:59.980
All the things I told were lies.
我刚才说的全都是谎话。

815
00:36:00.220 --> 00:36:00.600
No.
不会吧。

816
00:36:00.820 --> 00:36:02.500
Joel, you stinker.
乔尔，你这个淘气鬼。

817
00:36:03.120 --> 00:36:03.980
All right, bud.
好啦，兄弟。

818
00:36:04.100 --> 00:36:04.620
Thank you.
谢谢你。

819
00:36:04.620 --> 00:36:05.640
I'll talk to you soon.
我们回头聊。

820
00:36:05.860 --> 00:36:06.560
See you, guys.
再见啦，各位。

821
00:36:06.560 --> 00:36:07.520
Thank you.
谢谢。

822
00:36:07.820 --> 00:36:07.870
Bye.
拜拜。

823
00:36:16.180 --> 00:36:18.260
Hi, I'm Jessica St. Clair.
嗨，我是杰西卡·圣克莱尔。

824
00:36:18.580 --> 00:36:19.940
And I'm June Diane Raphael.
我是琼·黛安·拉斐尔。

825
00:36:20.080 --> 00:36:26.200
And we are two friends trying to survive the chaos and celebrate the joy that life throws our way.
我们是两个努力在生活中经历的混乱中求生存、并庆祝生活带给我们的喜悦的朋友。

826
00:36:26.320 --> 00:36:29.480
And we do it every week on our podcast, The Deep Dive.
每周我们都会在我们的播客《深度畅谈》中这样做。

827
00:36:29.700 --> 00:36:33.920
Sometimes we dig into the deep stuff, like how I communicate with my dead best friend.
有时我们会深入探讨沉重的话题，比如我是如何与我死去的挚友交流的。

828
00:36:34.220 --> 00:36:37.960
And sometimes we give bad advice based off a TikTok I saw.
有时我们则根据我在 TikTok 上看到的内容给出糟糕的建议。

829
00:36:38.180 --> 00:36:40.040
And we're not going to apologize for that.
而且我们对此绝不道歉。

830
00:36:40.200 --> 00:36:41.120
Absolutely not.
绝对不会。

831
00:36:41.120 --> 00:36:44.720
You'll laugh, you'll cry, and you'll hire a psychic medium.
你会大笑，你会流泪，你还会去雇一个灵媒。

832
00:36:45.120 --> 00:36:46.080
Join us, won't you?
加入我们，好吗？

833
00:36:46.260 --> 00:36:49.760
Listen to The Deep Dive wherever you get your podcasts from Lemonada Media.
在 Lemonada Media 收听你获取播客的任意平台上的《深度畅谈》。

834
00:36:50.200 --> 00:36:59.940
We are back.
我们回来了。

835
00:37:00.120 --> 00:37:04.320
We are back from playing Two Lies and a Truth with Joel McHale.
我们和乔尔·麦克海尔玩完“两假一真”游戏回来了。

836
00:37:04.320 --> 00:37:05.500
I told you.
我早就告诉你了。

837
00:37:05.640 --> 00:37:08.100
I knew when I was like, you never know what you're going to get.
我之前就觉得，你永远不知道会发生什么。

838
00:37:08.260 --> 00:37:12.020
We had no idea he was going to flip the script on us, but that was really fun.
我们完全没想到他会突然把局势反转，但这真的太好玩了。

839
00:37:12.760 --> 00:37:15.800
Well, could we get a little around the town?
那么，我们可以开始“走遍小镇”了吗？

840
00:37:16.920 --> 00:37:18.180
Around the town.
走遍小镇。

841
00:37:19.460 --> 00:37:23.820
Our first news item comes from Don T in Litton, British Columbia.
我们的第一条新闻来自不列颠哥伦比亚省利顿的唐·T。

842
00:37:24.200 --> 00:37:24.860
Don says,
唐说：

843
00:37:25.100 --> 00:37:29.900
Hey, Angela and Jenna, I live in a very small Canadian town along the Fraser River,
嘿，安吉拉和珍娜，我住在弗雷泽河畔一个非常小的加拿大城镇，

844
00:37:29.900 --> 00:37:36.500
and we have a little two-car ferry that I have to go on to get across the river to get to work.
我们有一艘小型双车渡轮，我必须坐它过河去上班。

845
00:37:36.980 --> 00:37:42.200
Lately, there have been a lot of large ice chunks floating down the river,
最近，河里漂流着很多大冰块，

846
00:37:42.200 --> 00:37:44.760
and this caused the paddle to break.
这导致螺旋桨坏了。

847
00:37:44.760 --> 00:37:49.960
So the ferry shut down for a while, but it's back and running as usual now.
所以渡轮停运了一段时间，不过现在已经恢复正常运行了。

848
00:37:50.260 --> 00:37:51.640
Wow, that's so wild to me.
哇，这对我来说太疯狂了。

849
00:37:51.840 --> 00:37:55.540
Just seeing huge chunks of ice floating, that's so wild.
光是看到巨大的冰块在漂浮，就觉得太不可思议了。

850
00:37:56.060 --> 00:38:00.600
All right, our next around the town is from Stephanie Z in St. Louis, Jenna.
好的，我们的下一个“走遍小镇”来自圣路易斯的斯蒂芬妮·Z，珍娜。

851
00:38:00.960 --> 00:38:01.760
Hi, Stephanie.
嗨，斯蒂芬妮。

852
00:38:02.160 --> 00:38:03.040
Stephanie said,
斯蒂芬妮说，

853
00:38:03.180 --> 00:38:06.580
This week for Valentine's Day, we're seeing something very dear to my heart.
本周的情人节，我们要看一些对我来说非常珍贵的东西。

854
00:38:06.700 --> 00:38:09.940
There's a great entertainer, Clownvis Presley,
有一位伟大的艺人，小丑埃尔维斯·普雷斯利，

855
00:38:10.140 --> 00:38:13.600
playing a set of love songs in his style at the City Museum.
将在城市博物馆用他的风格表演一系列情歌。

856
00:38:14.320 --> 00:38:18.820
I've been seeing his live shows for over 10 years, and he's a local legend.
我观看他的现场演出已经超过10年了，他是个当地的传奇。

857
00:38:19.240 --> 00:38:24.160
The first time I visited this beautiful city was in 2021 to see one of his shows.
我第一次来到这座美丽的城市是在2021年，为了看他的一场演出。

858
00:38:24.460 --> 00:38:27.660
The year after that, I traveled here solo for another one,
在那之后的第二年，我独自一人来这里看另一场，

859
00:38:28.080 --> 00:38:31.280
met my partner at a show, and then I moved here in 2022.
在演出现场遇到了我的伴侣，然后我在2022年搬到了这里。

860
00:38:31.760 --> 00:38:36.340
We now have a charming little house in South City and five adorable cats.
我们现在在南城有一栋迷人的小房子和五只可爱的猫。

861
00:38:36.700 --> 00:38:39.620
Neither of us really celebrates this holiday too much,
我们俩其实都不怎么庆祝这个节日，

862
00:38:39.740 --> 00:38:42.840
but it's become our cute slash weird little tradition.
但这已经成了我们可爱又奇特的小传统。

863
00:38:42.840 --> 00:38:46.400
It's also really fun to explore the City Museum at night.
晚上探索城市博物馆也真的很有趣。

864
00:38:47.300 --> 00:38:49.440
Stephanie, this is so cool.
斯蒂芬妮，这太酷了。

865
00:38:49.660 --> 00:38:53.140
The last time I was in St. Louis with my family, we went to City Museum.
我上次和家人在圣路易斯时，我们去了城市博物馆。

866
00:38:53.920 --> 00:38:56.160
Angela, it's like no place I've ever been.
安吉拉，那地方跟我去过的任何地方都不一样。

867
00:38:56.320 --> 00:38:58.720
It's like five stories and a roof.
它有大约五层楼高，还有一个屋顶。

868
00:38:58.900 --> 00:39:04.320
It is filled with caves and caverns and crawl spaces
里面充满了山洞、洞穴和狭小的爬行空间，

869
00:39:04.320 --> 00:39:11.380
in a giant sculpture of a whale, and you just walk through all of it and climb through all of it.
在一个巨大的鲸鱼雕塑里，你可以直接在里面走来走去，到处攀爬。

870
00:39:11.500 --> 00:39:16.040
But then they also have this tank where you can put your hand in and all the fish come over
但他们还有一个水槽，你可以把手伸进去，所有的鱼都会聚过来，

871
00:39:16.040 --> 00:39:18.020
and like eat the dead skin off your hand.
就像吃掉你手上的死皮一样。

872
00:39:18.180 --> 00:39:18.840
Oh my goodness.
哦天哪。

873
00:39:19.700 --> 00:39:24.980
It's so cool and unique, and I didn't think it could get more unique.
这太酷太独特了，我没想到它还能变得更独特。

874
00:39:25.160 --> 00:39:29.060
But now I'm hearing that this past Valentine's Day, they had Clownvis Presley.
但现在我听说就在刚过去的情年节，他们请来了小丑埃尔维斯·普雷斯利。

875
00:39:29.060 --> 00:39:30.220
I had no idea.
我完全不知道。

876
00:39:30.480 --> 00:39:31.780
This place is really cool.
这个地方真的很酷。

877
00:39:31.960 --> 00:39:32.780
That is so cool.
那真是太酷了。

878
00:39:32.920 --> 00:39:35.980
Well, our last Around the Town comes from Mandy L.
好的，我们最后一个“走遍全城”栏目来自宾夕法尼亚州韦恩市的曼迪·L。

879
00:39:36.160 --> 00:39:37.200
in Wayne, Pennsylvania.
曼迪说，

880
00:39:37.660 --> 00:39:38.540
Mandy says,
我为我的侄女感到无比骄傲。

881
00:39:38.760 --> 00:39:40.780
I'm just bursting with pride for my niece.
海登·A小姐

882
00:39:41.100 --> 00:39:42.180
Miss Hayden A.
在学校排演的《贱女孩青春版》中被选中出演海伦太太一角。

883
00:39:42.320 --> 00:39:45.060
has been cast as the role of Mrs. Heron
这个角色最初由安娜·加斯泰尔小姐塑造，

884
00:39:45.060 --> 00:39:48.140
in her school's rendition of Mean Girls Jr.
最近又由珍娜·费舍尔小姐在大银幕上扮演，

885
00:39:48.920 --> 00:39:51.520
The role was originated by Miss Anna Gasteyer
祝海登·A小姐演出大获成功。

886
00:39:51.520 --> 00:39:54.820
and more recently played on the big screen by Miss Jenna Fisher,
哦，海登，祝你饰演海伦太太演出成功。

887
00:39:55.100 --> 00:39:57.840
wishing many broken legs to Miss Hayden A.
我演那个角色时可喜欢了。

888
00:39:58.460 --> 00:40:02.620
Oh, Hayden, break a leg as Mrs. Heron.
那是个好角色。

889
00:40:02.840 --> 00:40:03.980
I loved playing that part.
好的，非常感谢大家发来“走遍全城”的内容。

890
00:40:04.140 --> 00:40:04.780
It's a good part.
现在我们要用本周的办公室问题来做个总结。

891
00:40:05.120 --> 00:40:08.080
Well, thank you so much for sending in your Around the Towns.
这个问题来自奥尔巴尼的克雷格·W。

892
00:40:08.180 --> 00:40:11.620
And now we're going to wrap things up with our office question of the week.
克雷格想知道，

893
00:40:11.980 --> 00:40:13.700
This comes from Craig W.
当演员们笑得停不下来时，谁是那个能镇住全场的大人？

894
00:40:13.960 --> 00:40:14.640
in Albany.
大家是怎么从具有传染性的傻笑中恢复过来的？

895
00:40:15.140 --> 00:40:16.500
Craig wants to know,
哦，克雷格。

896
00:40:16.680 --> 00:40:21.000
who was the grown-up in the room when the cast lost it for too long?
克雷格，这是个好问题。

897
00:40:21.320 --> 00:40:24.820
How was everyone brought back from contagious giggles?
哦，克雷格。

898
00:40:25.700 --> 00:40:26.480
Oh, Craig.
哦，克雷格。

899
00:40:26.480 --> 00:40:28.120
Craig, this is a good question.
哦，克雷格。

900
00:40:28.460 --> 00:40:29.200
Oh, Craig.
哦，克雷格。

901
00:40:29.480 --> 00:40:30.320
I can tell you what.
我跟你直说吧。

902
00:40:30.400 --> 00:40:31.040
It wasn't me.
不是我。

903
00:40:31.240 --> 00:40:31.920
That's what I can tell you.
这就是我想说的。

904
00:40:31.920 --> 00:40:32.840
It wasn't me.
不是我。

905
00:40:33.220 --> 00:40:35.740
Who brought us back to being serious?
是谁把我们拉回严肃状态的？

906
00:40:36.480 --> 00:40:39.320
I can definitely tell you all the people it wasn't.
我绝对可以告诉你所有不是的人。

907
00:40:39.560 --> 00:40:41.200
It was not John Krasinski.
不是约翰·卡拉辛斯基。

908
00:40:41.420 --> 00:40:42.320
It was not Angela.
不是安吉拉。

909
00:40:42.640 --> 00:40:43.380
It was not me.
不是我。

910
00:40:43.620 --> 00:40:44.540
It was not Mindy.
不是敏迪。

911
00:40:44.540 --> 00:40:46.680
It was definitely not Mindy.
绝对不是敏迪。

912
00:40:46.860 --> 00:40:47.760
It was definitely not Mindy.
绝对不是敏迪。

913
00:40:48.300 --> 00:40:53.400
Maybe a director would step in and try to wrangle us.
也许导演会介入并试图管束我们。

914
00:40:53.860 --> 00:40:59.240
Every once in a while, I know over in accounting, when Brian and I would get the giggles, Oscar would be like, come on, guys.
偶尔，我知道在会计部门那边，每当我和布赖恩忍不住傻笑时，奥斯卡就会说，行了，伙计们。

915
00:40:59.480 --> 00:40:59.980
Come on.
行了。

916
00:41:02.240 --> 00:41:06.240
So, sometimes Oscar, but yeah, it was hard.
所以，有时是奥斯卡，不过是的，这很难。

917
00:41:06.240 --> 00:41:10.360
It was really difficult not to laugh, and we often ruin many takes.
要忍住不笑真的很难，而且我们经常毁掉很多条拍摄。

918
00:41:10.360 --> 00:41:12.380
But it was also the crew.
但也有剧组人员的原因。

919
00:41:12.880 --> 00:41:20.280
I mean, sometimes you could just see Matt and Randall kind of like shaking with the camera on their shoulder.
我是说，有时候你能看到马特和兰德尔扛着摄像机肩膀都在发抖。

920
00:41:20.620 --> 00:41:26.380
Or especially if you had a writer like Jen Salata, she would ruin so many takes herself.
或者特别是如果你有一个像珍·萨拉塔这样的编剧，她自己就会毁掉无数条拍摄。

921
00:41:26.800 --> 00:41:29.240
Just as the writer-producer off-camera.
就在镜头外作为编剧兼制片人。

922
00:41:29.620 --> 00:41:30.080
Yeah.
是啊。

923
00:41:30.560 --> 00:41:33.160
And Greg, too, though, and Paul.
还有格雷格，以及保罗。

924
00:41:33.380 --> 00:41:33.680
Yeah.
是啊。

925
00:41:33.820 --> 00:41:41.100
I feel like in terms of people who were off-camera who would break and then get us going, and then it's hard to come back from that,
我觉得就那些在镜头外会笑场然后把我们也带笑，接着就很难再进入状态的人来说，

926
00:41:41.220 --> 00:41:44.560
especially when you've made the off-camera people laugh, too.
特别是当你连镜头外的人都逗笑了的时候。

927
00:41:45.000 --> 00:41:46.920
Well, that's the biggest win, right?
嗯，那才是最大的胜利，对吧？

928
00:41:47.100 --> 00:41:54.800
I remember one time watching our boom operator, Nick Carbone, his handshake as he held the boom because he was laughing.
我记得有一次看到我们的杆式话筒员尼克·卡尔博尼，他因为在笑，拿着话筒的手都在抖。

929
00:41:54.800 --> 00:41:57.340
His, like, shoulders were going, and I was like, yes!
他的肩膀一耸一耸的，当时我就想，太棒了！

930
00:41:58.520 --> 00:41:59.200
But yeah.
不过是的。

931
00:41:59.540 --> 00:42:01.660
Well, Craig, thank you so much for your question.
嗯，克雷グ，非常感谢你的提问。

932
00:42:01.660 --> 00:42:04.640
It definitely brought a smile to my face remembering all of that.
想起这一切，确实让我脸上露出了笑容。

933
00:42:04.760 --> 00:42:12.760
But I guess our answer is the directors usually had to rein us in, and every once in a while, Oscar, under his breath, would be like, come on, guys.
但我想我们的答案是，通常导演不得不把我们管束住，而且偶尔，奥斯卡会压低声音说，行了，伙计们。

934
00:42:12.980 --> 00:42:18.520
And maybe Kelly Cantley could get us to pull it together, right?
也许凯利·坎特利能让我们收敛一点，对吧？

935
00:42:18.580 --> 00:42:18.840
Yeah.
是啊。

936
00:42:19.260 --> 00:42:19.700
Or AD.
或者助理导演。

937
00:42:20.040 --> 00:42:20.240
Yeah.
是啊。

938
00:42:20.240 --> 00:42:20.960
Maybe Kelly.
也许是凯利。

939
00:42:21.440 --> 00:42:22.200
I think so.
我想是的。

940
00:42:22.200 --> 00:42:25.460
She would sometimes come in and be like, guys, do we want to make it to lunch?
她有时会走过来对我们说，伙计们，我们还想不想吃午饭了？

941
00:42:25.640 --> 00:42:26.420
Let's make it.
加把劲吧。

942
00:42:26.880 --> 00:42:27.180
Yeah.
是啊。

943
00:42:27.560 --> 00:42:30.460
Bring up food, and that could get us to become serious.
提一下食物，这就能让我们变得严肃起来。

944
00:42:31.000 --> 00:42:45.160
Lady, do you remember early on, before Nick Carbone joined us, and it might have even been someone who was just on set as, like, an extra set of hands, there was a boom operator.
女士，你还记得早期吗？在尼克·卡尔博尼加入我们之前，甚至可能只是某个在片场搭把手的人，当时有个杆式话筒员。

945
00:42:47.320 --> 00:42:51.740
And we were laughing, and he got really annoyed with us.
我们在笑，他变得非常生我们的气。

946
00:42:51.900 --> 00:42:52.740
Do you remember that?
你还记得吗？

947
00:42:52.920 --> 00:42:53.960
It was in the kitchen.
那是在厨房里。

948
00:42:54.200 --> 00:42:58.500
We were in the kitchen, and I think I'm thinking of the episode, but I don't want to say what it is.
我们在厨房里，我想我记得是哪一集，但我不想说出来是哪集。

949
00:42:58.800 --> 00:43:04.940
And we were all busting up laughing, and he got super annoyed, and I thought, man, this is not the job for you.
我们当时都笑得前俯后仰，他超级生气，当时我想，天哪，这工作真不适合你。

950
00:43:05.580 --> 00:43:07.340
Like, this is part of it.
这本来就是工作的一部分。

951
00:43:07.340 --> 00:43:09.280
Like, we're making comedy here.
就好像，我们在拍喜剧。

952
00:43:09.280 --> 00:43:12.520
We're going to break sometimes, and that's part of the energy.
我们有时会笑场，这也是那种氛围的一部分。

953
00:43:12.860 --> 00:43:17.620
And I think he didn't find the show as funny as the rest of us.
我觉得他觉得这节目没我们其他人觉得那么好笑。

954
00:43:17.620 --> 00:43:19.140
I don't think he thought it was funny.
我觉得他觉得这并不好笑。

955
00:43:19.380 --> 00:43:19.780
Yeah.
没错。

956
00:43:20.080 --> 00:43:20.780
I do.
我觉得是的。

957
00:43:20.900 --> 00:43:21.700
I remember him.
我记得他。

958
00:43:21.800 --> 00:43:23.660
But, yeah, our show wasn't for him.
不过，也是，我们的节目不适合他。

959
00:43:23.780 --> 00:43:24.300
It wasn't.
确实不适合。

960
00:43:24.340 --> 00:43:27.100
He needed to be on a drama, something more serious.
他需要去演正剧，一些更严肃的剧。

961
00:43:27.340 --> 00:43:28.440
A procedural, yeah.
律政或刑侦剧吧，对。

962
00:43:28.960 --> 00:43:30.100
He wasn't loving it.
他并不怎么享受。

963
00:43:30.220 --> 00:43:32.760
But listen, I mean, that comes with the territory on a comedy.
但听着，我的意思是，拍喜剧就是这样的。

964
00:43:32.760 --> 00:43:39.320
I feel like that's something that I learned, too, is that the atmosphere of making a comedy is comedic.
我觉得这也是我学到的一点，那就是拍喜剧的氛围本身就是喜剧性的。

965
00:43:39.500 --> 00:43:47.340
And if you get too serious or you're just constantly looking at the clock and you're, like, wondering when are we going to get this shot, like,
如果你变得太严肃，或者总是在看表，然后，比如说，在想我们什么时候能拍完这个镜头，就像是，

966
00:43:47.380 --> 00:43:58.900
that's actually a hard role for our first ADs, for Kelly and for Rusty, because they have to leave time for the levity on set to keep the comedy ball in the air.
这对我们的第一副导演凯莉和拉斯蒂来说其实是个很难的角色，因为他们必须留出时间让片场保持轻松，好让喜剧的节奏持续下去。

967
00:43:58.900 --> 00:44:05.620
But you also have to make sure you're getting the shot and that we're breaking in time for lunch and all that kind of stuff.
但你同时也得确保拍到了镜头，确保我们能在午饭前收工之类的各种事情。

968
00:44:05.820 --> 00:44:14.960
And so we were really lucky with Kelly and Rusty because they let us have fun, but they were pretty good at, like, reining us in when they needed to as well.
所以我们在凯莉和拉斯蒂身上真的很幸运，因为他们让我们玩得很开心，但在需要的时候，他们也很擅长把我们拉回正轨。

969
00:44:15.540 --> 00:44:20.540
Yeah, they were like your fun aunt and uncle, you know, that let you, like, just let loose.
对，他们就像是你有趣的叔叔阿姨，你知道的，就让你彻底放松。

970
00:44:20.680 --> 00:44:22.380
But then it was like, all right, guys, come on.
但接着就会像是，好了，各位，来吧。

971
00:44:22.560 --> 00:44:23.160
Let's go.
我们走。

972
00:44:23.440 --> 00:44:23.700
Yeah.
是啊。

973
00:44:24.260 --> 00:44:24.500
Yeah.
对。

974
00:44:24.600 --> 00:44:26.000
You can't stay up too late.
你们不能熬夜太晚。

975
00:44:26.380 --> 00:44:27.040
That's right.
没错。

976
00:44:28.900 --> 00:44:29.400
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

977
00:44:29.580 --> 00:44:29.840
Yeah.
是啊。

978
00:44:30.860 --> 00:44:34.900
Some of the times I laughed so hard, too, was just in the pauses.
有时我笑得最厉害的时候，其实是在停顿的间隙。

979
00:44:35.280 --> 00:44:44.120
I don't know if you remember that, Jenna, but there were so many times when we were in a conference room and Steve as Michael would start improvising.
我不知道你还记不记得，珍娜，但有太多次我们在会议室里，史蒂夫饰演的迈克尔会开始即兴发挥。

980
00:44:44.120 --> 00:44:45.760
So we didn't know what he was about to say.
所以我们根本不知道他接下来要说什么。

981
00:44:45.900 --> 00:44:48.460
We'd already gotten the scene scripted many times.
剧本上的戏我们已经拍过很多遍了。

982
00:44:48.660 --> 00:44:57.140
And then there'd be one or two moments where Steve as Michael would have a list of things he had to say and he would start improvising that liSt.
然后会有一两个时刻，史蒂夫饰演的迈克尔会有一串他必须说的话，接着他就会开始即兴发挥那一长串内容。

983
00:44:57.540 --> 00:45:03.560
And it was the pause before he said the next thing where I would come undone.
就是他在说下一句之前的那段停顿，让我彻底破防了。

984
00:45:03.780 --> 00:45:08.100
The excitement of what he was going to say was so thrilling to me.
对他说出口的话的期待让我感到无比兴奋。

985
00:45:08.280 --> 00:45:11.840
And then inevitably, whatever he said would be ridiculously funny.
然后不可避免地，他说出的任何话都会荒谬地好笑。

986
00:45:12.020 --> 00:45:17.520
But it was the pause that got me, like, his long, like, I'm like, oh, my God, I'm out.
但真正击中我的是那个停顿，比如他长长的，我就想，天哪，我不行了。

987
00:45:17.640 --> 00:45:18.060
I'm out.
我彻底笑趴了。

988
00:45:18.060 --> 00:45:22.860
All of this reminiscing about this is just, gosh, we laughed a lot.
所有这些回忆，天哪，我们以前真的笑得太多了。

989
00:45:23.160 --> 00:45:29.480
What a gift that our job was to go somewhere and be around funny people being funny.
我们的工作居然是去某个地方，和一群搞笑的人在一起搞笑，这真是上帝的恩赐。

990
00:45:29.840 --> 00:45:31.500
There's just nothing like it.
简直无与伦比。

991
00:45:32.040 --> 00:45:32.600
Truly.
真的。

992
00:45:33.020 --> 00:45:33.920
We're really lucky.
我们真的很幸运。

993
00:45:34.860 --> 00:45:35.100
Yeah.
是啊。

994
00:45:35.760 --> 00:45:37.400
Oh, you guys, thank you so much.
哦，伙计们，非常感谢。

995
00:45:37.540 --> 00:45:39.140
We hope you enjoyed this episode.
我们希望你们喜欢这一集。

996
00:45:39.140 --> 00:45:43.560
Big thank you to Joel McHale for spending the afternoon with us, being silly.
非常感谢乔尔·麦克海尔和我们度过了一个下午，陪我们一起搞笑。

997
00:45:44.120 --> 00:45:48.620
And thank you to everyone who sends in their chit-chats and around the towns.
也要感谢所有发来闲聊和周边趣闻的每一个人。

998
00:45:48.880 --> 00:45:51.120
We love hearing from you guys so much.
我们非常喜欢听到你们的分享。

999
00:45:51.220 --> 00:45:53.880
We appreciate this community so very much.
我们极其感激这个社区。

1000
00:45:54.020 --> 00:46:02.160
And just in case these kittens are still in my house, everybody, please go to kittenrescue.org and adopt my kittens.
以防万一这些小猫还在我家里，各位，请去 kittenrescue.org 领养我的小猫吧。

1001
00:46:02.640 --> 00:46:04.700
Yes, adoption of sweet kittens.
没错，收养可爱的小猫咪。

1002
00:46:05.100 --> 00:46:07.260
All right, you guys, have a great week.
好了，各位，祝你们度过愉快的一周。

1003
00:46:07.260 --> 00:46:08.480
We'll see you next time.
我们下期再见。

1004
00:46:08.740 --> 00:46:09.240
See you then.
到时候见。

1005
00:46:09.640 --> 00:46:14.820
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies.
感谢收听《办公室女士》。

1006
00:46:15.140 --> 00:46:20.200
Office Ladies is a presentation of Odyssey and is produced by Jenna Fisher and Angela Kinsey.
《办公室女士》是由奥德赛公司呈现，珍娜·费舍和安吉拉·金西制作。

1007
00:46:20.400 --> 00:46:22.420
Our senior producer is Matt Beagle.
我们的资深制作人是马特·比格尔。

1008
00:46:22.680 --> 00:46:24.620
And our audio engineer is Sam Kiefer.
我们的音频工程师是萨姆·基弗。

1009
00:46:24.900 --> 00:46:27.460
Odyssey's executive producer is Leah Reese Dennis.
奥德赛公司的执行制作人是莉亚·里斯·丹尼斯。

1010
00:46:27.880 --> 00:46:30.700
Office Ladies was mixed and mastered by Bill Schultz.
《办公室女士》由比尔·舒尔茨进行混音和母带制作。

1011
00:46:30.840 --> 00:46:33.680
Our theme song is Rubber Tree by Creed Bratton.
我们的主题曲是克里德·布拉顿演奏的《橡胶树》。
